From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:59:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: bring the modem up, and stop rild crashing on the way

Two halves of one problem: this device has no working peripheral manager, and the radio depended on
it for two separate things.

First, rild crashed. BpPeripheralManager::registar() in the 2016 libperipheral_client.so
stack-allocates two android::Parcel objects 0x68 bytes apart, because that was sizeof(Parcel) in
2016. It is now at least 0x70 -- Parcel::Parcel() ends with "str xzr, [x0, #0x68]" -- and no ether
branch sets BOARD_VNDK_VERSION, so the blob links against the current libbinder and that store lands
exactly on registar's stack canary. It aborted in the prologue on every call, before any binder
traffic. 100 tombstones, all rild, until init gave up restarting it.

  Abort message: 'stack corruption detected (-fstack-protector)'
  #02 libperipheral_client.so (BpPeripheralManager::registar)
  #05 libril-qc-qmi-1.so (qmi_ril_peripheral_mng_init+608)
  #07 libril-qc-qmi-1.so (RIL_Init+84)

libshims_peripheral_client reports failure from the five pm_client_* entry points, shimmed onto
libril-qc-qmi-1.so alone so pm-service, pm-proxy and liblbs_core keep the real library. Failure is
true -- vendor.qcom.PeripheralManager never registers -- and it is a path the RIL was written for:
qmi_ril_peripheral_mng_init tests the return with cbz, and its caller with cbnz, and skips the ESOC
setup the Robin's internal modem does not have.

Second, nobody booted the modem. That was peripheral manager's other job, and skipping the ESOC path
does not restore it -- the subsystem was already never booting while rild was crash-looping at that
same call. The whole radio stack then stalls waiting on a subsystem that is OFFLINE:

  linux_qmi_qmux_io.c: Unable to open port id /dev/smdcntl0, error [110:Connection timed out]
  qmi_client: unable to connect to server, errno=[2:No such file or directory], attempt=49

ether_modem_hold opens /dev/subsys_modem, which is subsystem_get("modem"), and holds it. Verified by
hand on the device: the subsystem goes ONLINE, PIL loads the firmware, and the rest follows without
any other change -- smdcntl0 appears, the qmux sockets are created, and rild services RIL requests
(qcril_qmi_nas_get_cell_info_list_ncl completed with 39).

It is a separate service rather than something in the shim because /dev/subsys_modem is 0640 system
system and rild is uid radio, so rild cannot open it -- sepolicy already allows it, DAC does not. It
runs in class core so the modem is up before qmuxd's first open instead of after it has started
retrying.

Cellular is still untested; there is no SIM in the device. This makes the radio stack come up at all,
which it never has on this branch.
---
 BoardConfig.mk                                |  1 +
 device.mk                                     |  2 +
 libshims/Android.mk                           | 11 +++
 .../peripheral_client/peripheral_client.c     | 67 +++++++++++++++++
 modem_hold/Android.mk                         | 27 +++++++
 modem_hold/modem_hold.c                       | 72 +++++++++++++++++++
 rootdir/init.target.rc                        |  5 ++
 sepolicy/file_contexts                        |  3 +
 sepolicy/modem_hold.te                        |  9 +++
 9 files changed, 197 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libshims/peripheral_client/peripheral_client.c
 create mode 100644 modem_hold/Android.mk
 create mode 100644 modem_hold/modem_hold.c
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/modem_hold.te

